        {
            "id": "50c5cef3-73ba-428b-a866-f3fde03e3193",
            "build_id": "f6e6378e-37ce-49b6-af72-935936834a83",
            "round_number": 5,
            "cash_earned": 0,
            "created_at": "2025-09-19T20:13:27.376822+00:00",
            "notes": "[Quantum Clip](item_3a108115-ec6e-4b98-8074-1b015cf535f1) is the power I like to go here because, once again, ammo is very good on Tracer and its gives us 25%. It also gives us weapon lifesteal, which synergizes with phantasmic flux, as another benefit.\n\n\nI haven't solved what late game weapon items are best, but [Underworld Quickloader](item_dc8e93b1-a561-4007-bfdc-42839f612d01) is strong as it cuts your downtime from reloading by 30%, with good damaging stats still there with the weapon power and attack speed. \n\nI could see these items also being good this round too, but now we are looking at either marginal differences, what you can afford based on cash, or the best order to buy them.\n## Standout Items\n-  [Weapon Jammer](item_72386db6-753e-413d-aa2a-f1389842f47f) Since it we use so much attack speed, that the 10% attack speed increase is around equivalent to 10% weapon power, so this is pretty much giving us 20%wp and 19 armor, which is really good for how much it costs.\n- [Hardlight Accelerator](item_0390c8af-2a68-4da2-b876-93da32c3f448) We like cdr, and we will very likely have 20% or 25% weapon power at most times.\n## Slightly worse choices for the cost\n- [Eye of the Spider](item_bbaf01d7-340d-4199-b738-86a98d68fe9b) The highest weapon power numbers, but expensive.\n- [The Closer](item_173c6d0f-dbe6-440e-924f-0ce08189ddce) Expensive, but good damage numbers and also good utility via revealing enemies to your teammates.\n\n\n## Why I don't like some powers\n- We want to use recall like a normal recall, to keep ourselves alive, so the powers that add to recall just encourage us to use it at awkward times, so I don't think [Alternate Ending](item_746b8915-22ff-4521-bc52-71b4edb630c6), [Bullet Time](item_6840382c-ae92-491a-b70c-b49f3a76003a), or [Temportal](item_8564184d-a729-4f8a-afa2-168995c35152) are very consistent.\n- We don't want to be meleeing all that much, so the melee powers [Flash Fist](item_418a92bd-1b45-4135-aca0-682d3c7a845b) and [Get Stuffed!](item_3b0530be-462d-4e2d-8b4d-05c027d6aa60) are off the table\n- [Foresight](item_f4163ce1-8f80-43ca-85d4-39812084400f) affects very few bullets, and doesn't really give us numbers like [Quantum Clip](item_3a108115-ec6e-4b98-8074-1b015cf535f1). And the [Timelapse](item_20d43db5-d2ad-47e9-b32f-82d8eca006ce) numbers are also underwhelming compared to it as well.",
